{"id": "swebq0120", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The government in Virginia Colony was a representative democracy, which means that citizens elected officials to make decisions for them. This system allowed people to have some control over how the colony was run. However, there were also laws and rules that everyone had to follow, just like today. So while they could vote and choose leaders, they still had to obey certain guidelines set by the government.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
