{"id": "swebq0216", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The ancient Chinese writing system was a form of logographic script, meaning that each character represented either a word or a concept rather than a sound. It developed over thousands of years, with its earliest forms dating back to the Shang Dynasty around 1 600 BCE. These early characters were inscribed on bone s and shells using tools like cu es and drills. Over time, the script evolved into more complex forms during the Zhou and Qin dynasties. One significant development was the standard ization of characters under Emperor Qin Shi Huang in the third century BCE, which helped unify communication across the vast empire. The characters continued to refine through subsequent dyn asties, eventually leading to modern standard s like Ka i and Song scripts. Despite changes, many ancient characters are still recognizable today, showing the enduring nature of this unique writing system.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 52, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "swebq0224", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In 2013, the two Virginia Senators were Mark R. Warner and Tim Kaine. Both served in the U S Senate during that year as representatives for the state of Virginia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
