{"id": "swebq0240", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Vietnam has some amazing beaches, and the best places to go really depend on what you're looking for. If you want a mix of culture, nature, and beach life, Ho Chi Minh City is a great starting point, but if you head down the coast, Nha Trang is one of the most popular spots. It has long stretches of white sand, clear water, and lots of resort s and activities like sc uba diving. Further south, Phu Quoc Island offers even more tranquility with its untouched coastline and fewer crowds. For something wilder and more remote, Ha Long Bay isn't technically a beach, but it's often paired with coastal travel. Nearby Cat Ba Island also has beautiful bays perfect for swimming and relax ing. If you prefer less touristy areas, the central coast like Da N ang or the lesser-known beaches around Hue can be fantastic for peace and quiet. The key is deciding whether you want lively beach town s or serene natural setting s. Either way, Vietnam’s coastline has something incredible for everyone.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 44, "carrier_ended": null}
